# {{ project_name }} instructions

Index for agents. Read the generated wiki index [generated/wiki/index.md](generated/wiki/index.md) first: one line per
capability, each page showing its requirements, the code that implements them and their tests (`uv run lockstep check
project` writes it; never edit it). Then [docs/index.md](docs/index.md), which lists the architecture, diagram,
requirements and decisions.{% if code2_workspace %} Workspace rules: `~/code2/AGENTS.md`.{% endif %}

- Each kind of document has one home, listed with what belongs there under `document_homes:` in
  `lockstep.yaml`: design in `docs/architecture/`, decisions in `docs/decisions/`, requirements and changes in
  `openspec/`, research in `research/`, observations in `evidence/`, generator output in `generated/`. A Markdown
  file anywhere else fails `make check`; move it, or declare a new home there.
- Behavior changes go through OpenSpec (`openspec/changes/<name>/`), then archive with
  `openspec archive <name> --yes`.
- Each change's `proposal.md` states its size on one line: `Plan size: small` (the change is the plan;
  the checks are the gate) or `Plan size: full` with a line `Planning package: <path>` naming its package
{% if code2_workspace %}  (`~/code2/workspace/agents/topics/working-method.md`, "A requirement change states its size").
{% endif %}  `lockstep check changed` in `make check` fails without it.
{% if code2_workspace -%}
- Every requirement and decision record carries a `Source:` line: `Source: Brian, <date>: "<his words>"`
  or `Source: inferred by agent (<basis>)`. Implementation (code, tests, diagram) is the agent's call; a
  significant requirement or decision an agent inferred is a working default: apply it and list it under
  "Decided by me, you can veto" in the reply. It waits for Brian's yes only when it is also uncertain and
  high-impact (`~/code2/AGENTS.md`, "Who decided"; Brian, 2026-11-16: "i approve 7 tight").
  `lockstep check sources` enforces the line.
{% else -%}
- Every requirement and decision record carries a `Source:` line: `Source: <owner>, <date>: "<their words>"`
  or `Source: inferred by agent (<basis>)`. Implementation (code, tests, diagram) is the agent's call; a
  significant requirement or decision an agent inferred is a working default: apply it and say so in the
  reply, so the owner can undo it. `lockstep check sources` enforces the line.
{% endif -%}
- Where `lockstep.yaml` holds `layout:` rows, a plan is the OpenSpec change plus a row for every new or changed file under
  `src/{{ package_name }}/` (path, purpose, the requirements it implements, its tests, its typed `exports`),
  committed together, spec first: a row naming an unknown requirement is refused. After the plan commit, run
  `uv run lockstep layout`: it creates each planned file with its requirement text in the docstring. The edit
  hook refuses a file with no row; `make check` runs the same whole-tree check. A refusal for a stale plan copy
  is fixed by `uv run lockstep check project`.
- Write the failing test before the code, marked `@pytest.mark.req("<capability>/<scenario>")`.
- The module that implements a requirement says `Implements: <capability>/<requirement>` in its
  docstring; in a planned file the generated plan text between the cog lines carries it from the layout row, and
  elsewhere continuation lines are indented.
- Change structure in `docs/architecture/model.c4`, then run `uv run lockstep check arch gen`.
  Never edit `.importlinter` by hand.
- `make fast` runs on commit and push. `ship` runs `make check` before merging.

## When a check refuses

Run the failing command again from the repository root after applying the fix.
`make check` first runs `make docs-specs` and `make fast`, then the merge checks below.
If a command is missing, install the named tool or run `uv sync` for a project dependency.

| Command or message | What to fix |
| --- | --- |
| `make docs-specs` | Keep each capability at `openspec/specs/<capability>/spec.md`. This target links those files into `docs/specs/`; check the destination permissions if it cannot write. |
| `lockstep check trace` | For an unimplemented requirement, list it in the module's layout row and regenerate. For an untested scenario, add a test with its `@pytest.mark.req("<capability>/<scenario>")` marker. Correct unknown IDs in the marker or implementation reference. |
| `lockstep check sources` | Add a `Source:` line that names the actual decision or states the basis for an inference. |
| `lockstep check project --check` | For `RESULT project stale=<n>`, run `uv run lockstep check project`, review the rewrites, and commit any tracked changes. |
| `lint-imports` | Move the dependency to an allowed direction. If the intended architecture changed, update the diagram and run `uv run lockstep check arch gen`. |
| `pydoclint src` | `DOC101`: document the missing arguments in the Google-style `Args:` section. `DOC201`: document the returned value in `Returns:`. `DOC301`: this template allows constructor docstrings; if the setting was lost, restore `allow-init-docstring = true` under `[tool.pydoclint]` so the constructor can also pass `interrogate`. |
| `interrogate src` | Add meaningful docstrings to the reported modules, classes or functions, including constructors. |
| `openspec validate --all --strict --no-interactive` | Correct the reported spec or change, including missing scenario headings or malformed delta sections. |
| `.code2check/` and `pytest --junitxml=.code2check/junit.xml` | Ensure the directory is writable. Fix the failing behavior or collection error in the pytest output, then rerun the check to produce a fresh report. |
| `lockstep check arch check` | Fix missing or invalid diagram entries or broken import contracts. Regenerate the import configuration from the diagram. |
| `lockstep check test-first --base origin/main` | For `no-failing-test`, cover the new or changed scenario with a marked test that fails on the base. Use `existing=True` only for a new scenario documenting behavior already present on the base. |
| `lockstep check changed --base origin/main` | Name the changed requirements in their plan. Add the required `Plan size:` declaration based on the project’s planning criteria. For a full plan, add `Planning package: <path>` pointing to a committed package. |
| `lockstep check suppressions --base origin/main` | Remove the new suppression or add a nearby comment explaining why it is necessary. |
| `lockstep check maintainability --base origin/main` | Address the cited growth or complexity. For a file beyond its limit, put cohesive new behavior in a planned module. |
| `lockstep check --repo . --base <ref>` | For `BLOCK`, correct the cited layout, projected text or public symbol. Add the missing file row or typed `exports:` entry before rerunning `uv run lockstep check project`. Keep internal helpers private. |
| `lockstep check project` | Fix the underlying spec, layout or file error it reports. This step refreshes generated evidence for the docs build. |
| `zensical build --strict` | Fix the named broken link, missing source or API symbol, or warning in the documentation config. Build again before merging. |

If the optional planning gate reports `FAIL cold_review: missing` or a stale review, have the planning
package reviewed independently and record the verdict and the revision read. A stale review alone
produces a warning if the package otherwise validates. Other failures follow the configured gate mode.
